meta {
  name: 9e. Verify Management API via Gateway (host-agnostic catch-all)
  type: http
  seq: 26
  tags: [
    requires-nifi
  ]
}

get {
  url: {{apisixGatewayHost}}/v1/datasets/{{sagaDataSetId}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  x-api-request: true
}

tests {
  test("sagaDataSetId is set by earlier steps", function() {
    expect(bru.getVar('sagaDataSetId'), "sagaDataSetId must be set").to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;
  });

  test("Management catch-all route is host-agnostic — not 404", function() {
    // apisixGatewayHost uses a Host that is NOT the API vhost (api.localhost). The dynamic
    // FROST data-plane route is bound to api.localhost, so this request must fall through to
    // the host-agnostic /v1/* management catch-all and reach portal-backend. A 404 means the
    // catch-all got host-bound again (the pre-fix regression, issue #1368).
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.not.equal(404);
  });

  test("Authenticated management request reaches the backend and returns the dataset", function() {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
    expect(res.body).to.have.property('id', bru.getVar('sagaDataSetId'));
  });
}

docs {
  **Saga step 9e of 18** — Verify the management API stays reachable through the gateway on any Host.

  Issue #1368 introduced an API virtual host (`api.localhost`) for the published data-plane and, in an early port, also bound the `/v1/*` management catch-all route to it. That broke the portal-frontend, whose server-side proxy strips the `Host` header and calls APISIX as `localhost:9080` — the bound route then 404s. The fix keeps the catch-all **host-agnostic** (only the dynamic per-dataset FROST routes are bound to the API vhost).

  This step pins that contract: it sends an authenticated GET to APISIX via `apisixGatewayHost` (a Host other than `api.localhost`) and asserts it reaches portal-backend and returns the dataset — not a 404 from a host mismatch.

  **Precondition:** `sagaDataSetId` set; APISIX reachable at `apisixGatewayHost`; the requesting user has DATASET_READ on the dataset.

  **Expected Response:** 200 OK with the dataset JSON. A 404 indicates the management catch-all was host-bound again.
}
